{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0002013807","cik":"0002013807","slug":"foxx-development-holdings-013807","name":"Foxx Development Holdings Inc.","ticker":"FOXX","exchanges":["Nasdaq","Nasdaq"],"sector":"Computer Communications Equipment","sic":"3576","country":"TX","website":"","listed_years":1.8,"first_annual":"2024-10-24","last_filing":"2026-07-29","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0002013807&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["Foxx Development Holdings Inc. files with the SEC under \"Computer Communications Equipment\", based in TX, and has been publicly reporting for 2 years.","It reported $57.0m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, down 23.9% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of -16.7%.","Listed on Nasdaq, Nasdaq, it is still consuming cash, with roughly 19 months of runway at the current burn."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Net cash of $3.1m against total assets of $28.1m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390026059591/0001213900-26-059591-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-059591"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-0.9% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390026059591/0001213900-26-059591-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-059591"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue fell 23.9% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390026059591/0001213900-26-059591-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-059591"},{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 1015.6% across 5 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390026059591/0001213900-26-059591-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-059591"},{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 5.8% to -16.7% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390026059591/0001213900-26-059591-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-059591"},{"text":"Gross margin is only -16.7%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390026059591/0001213900-26-059591-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-059591"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-391.9% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390026059591/0001213900-26-059591-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-059591"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $30.4m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390026059591/0001213900-26-059591-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-059591"},{"text":"About 19 months of cash at the current burn ($3.2m against $2.0m a year). A company that must raise is a company that raises on the buyer's terms.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390025112192/0001213900-25-112192-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-25-112192"},{"text":"Shareholders' equity is negative (-$47.8m) - liabilities exceed assets on the balance sheet.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390026059591/0001213900-26-059591-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-059591"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 14.1% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (27,412 shares across 9 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2013807/000121390026065814/0001213900-26-065814-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 0.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.0,"consecutive":2,"current":-0.167,"current_display":"-16.7%","threshold_display":"0.0%","fired":true,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -39.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.39,"consecutive":2,"current":-0.239,"current_display":"-23.9%","threshold_display":"-39.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"runway_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Cash runway falls below 12 months","metric":"runway_months","comparison":"below","threshold":12.0,"consecutive":1,"current":19.068,"current_display":"19 months","threshold_display":"12 months","fired":false,"rationale":"Below twelve months the company raises on whatever terms it can get, and that dilution lands on you.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":-0.009,"current_display":"-0.9%","thr